    38	<objective>
    39	Give the Code stage an explicit unattended decision-checkpoint policy: when the agent reaches a
    40	`decision` checkpoint with no operator available, resolve it by evaluating the presented options
    41	on their merits and record the reasoning — rather than taking whichever option happens to be
    42	listed first.
    43	
    44	Purpose: DECN-01 / 999.94. Verified this session at
    45	`~/.claude/gsd-core/workflows/execute-phase.md:1123`, the workflow DevFlow's Code prompt tells
    46	the agent to run says, verbatim: *"**decision** → Auto-spawn continuation agent with
    47	`{user_response}` = first option from checkpoint details."* Positional order is not merit.
    48	
    49	Output: one shared policy constant delivered identically to both agent families, with tests that
    50	pin its content and prove the assertions discriminate — plus a plainly stated limit on what those
    51	tests establish. Implements D-03 exactly as locked in 45-CONTEXT.md: a dedicated policy
    52	instruction layer in `code_stage_prompt`, extended to the sibling renderer so the two agent
    53	families cannot diverge.
    54	</objective>
