    71	## What this plan does NOT establish — read before accepting it
    72	
    73	D-03 locks the mechanism to a prompt-template change in `prompt.rs`. That mechanism has a
    74	ceiling, and this plan states it rather than letting a green test suite imply more than it proves:
    75	
    76	1. **A string-presence test proves the instruction was DELIVERED. It does not prove the agent
    77	   OBEYED it.** Every test in this plan asserts on the rendered prompt text. None of them
    78	   observes a model resolving a real checkpoint. There is no unit test that can close that gap.
    79	2. **This does not change `execute-phase.md`.** That file lives in `~/.claude/gsd-core/`, outside
    80	   this repository, and its `decision` branch still reads "first option from checkpoint details".
   100	  post-hoc gate resume. Task 1 records this boundary in a doc comment on the new constant so a
   101	  future reader does not delete one as a duplicate of the other.
   102	- **"Prompt instructions cannot override a hardcoded procedural step if GSD does not consult the
   103	  LLM" — INCORPORATED as a stated limitation, not as a code change.** See item 2 above. The
   104	  finding is correct and this plan cannot fix it from inside this repository; D-03 locks the
   105	  mechanism to `prompt.rs`. Recorded with a recommended upstream follow-up rather than silently
   106	  dropped.
   107	- **"Add test fixtures verifying option ordering and decision rationale recording" —
   108	  INCORPORATED WITH A CORRECTION.** Rendered-prompt tests cannot verify *option ordering
   109	  behaviour*, because no option list exists at render time — the checkpoint's options are
   110	  discovered by the agent at run time, inside GSD, not by DevFlow. What IS deterministically
   111	  testable, and what Task 2 asserts, is that the delivered text forbids positional selection and
   112	  requires the reasoning to be recorded. Claiming a prompt test verifies ordering behaviour would
   113	  be exactly the proxy-measurement error this project's CLAUDE.md warns about.
   114	
