   124	
   125	DECN-01's probe row came back `{"category":"unclassified","status":"unresolved"}`. Per the
   126	protocol an `unclassified` row is never auto-resolved with a backstop and never silently dropped:
   127	
   128	> **FLAGGED (DECN-01, unclassified/unresolved):** the probe could not classify DECN-01's edge
   129	> category, so no probe-derived acceptance criterion was authored into `must_haves.truths` from
   130	> it. This is a plausible miss rather than a plausible absence — a requirement about resolving
   131	> checkpoints without an operator has obvious edges (what happens when the options are
   132	> indistinguishable on merit? when there are zero options? when the checkpoint is malformed?),
   133	> and NONE of them are reachable from DevFlow's side, because DevFlow renders a prompt and never
   134	> parses the checkpoint. **Reviewer: confirm you accept that those edges belong to GSD-core, not
   135	> to this phase.**
   136	
