   205	
   206	    Write the new section's text to say, in prose, all of the following. Wording is yours; every
   207	    item must be present:
   208	    - When a `decision` checkpoint is reached and no operator is available, resolve it rather than
   209	      pausing — this run is unattended and nobody is coming.
   210	    - Choose by comparing the presented options against the phase's goal and constraints. Do not
   211	      choose an option because of its position in the list. State explicitly that the GSD workflow
   212	      being invoked describes selecting the first option, and that this instruction supersedes
