    90	Applied unconditionally, that has a collateral effect D-02 does not mention and this plan will
    91	not ship silently. Verified against live source this session:
    92	
    93	- `enforce_build_staleness` (`staleness.rs:324-333`) computes `combined_staleness` FIRST and
    94	  `is_self_dogfood_workspace(project_root)` SECOND. The predicate therefore runs against
    95	  **every** project DevFlow drives, not only DevFlow's own workspace. The self-dogfood flag only
    96	  decides whether a Stale verdict Blocks or merely Warns (`staleness_outcome`).
    97	- So an unconditional `crates/` rule would make a modified `src/main.rs` in an ordinary Rust
    98	  project — the standard Cargo layout, where nothing lives under `crates/` — classify as
    99	  not-build-affecting. That project silently loses its stale-build warning. DevFlow is published
   100	  to crates.io and drives other people's repositories; deleting a safety warning for all of them
   101	  to fix this repo's spike directory is not what AUTO-02 asks for.
   102	
   103	**Decision:** thread a `workspace_scoped: bool` — sourced from the existing
   104	`is_self_dogfood_workspace` — through the predicate chain. Inside DevFlow's own workspace the
   105	narrowed `crates/` rule applies (AUTO-02 satisfied); everywhere else today's broad rule is
   106	preserved byte-for-byte. This keeps ONE predicate with ONE rule, parameterized — it does not
   107	fork or reimplement `affects_compiled_binary`, which the D-07 comment at `staleness.rs:104-109`
   108	explicitly forbids.
   109	
   110	**Rejected alternative:** apply the narrowed rule unconditionally (the most literal reading of
   111	D-02). Rejected because of the collateral warning loss above. **Operator: if you want the
   112	literal unconditional reading instead, say so and this becomes a one-line change** — drop the
   113	parameter and hardcode `true`. This is flagged rather than decided silently.
   114	
   115	## Review incorporation (REVIEWS.md finding 2)
   116	
   117	- **"Must ensure exact matching for root build files and prefix matching for `crates/`" —
   118	  INCORPORATED** as the literal predicate rule in Task 1, with `crates-extras/` and
   119	  `vendor/crates/` as explicit negative controls proving prefix, not substring.
   120	- **"Write explicit unit tests with negative controls" — INCORPORATED** as Task 2, which adds
   121	  the FIRST direct unit tests `affects_compiled_binary` and `porcelain_tracked_path` have ever
   122	  had. Verified at source: neither has any direct test today; both are exercised only
   123	  indirectly through git-fixture tests.
   124	- **"Standardize path normalization before predicate evaluation" — PARTIALLY INCORPORATED, with
   125	  one sub-item explicitly REJECTED.** `porcelain_tracked_path` (`staleness.rs:166-173`) already
   126	  handles status bytes, `ORIG -> PATH` renames, and quoting; Task 2 pins each of those with a
   127	  direct test. The finding also asks to handle a leading `./` prefix. **Rejected:**
   128	  `git status --porcelain` does not emit `./`-prefixed paths, and `git diff --name-only` (the
   129	  other input, `staleness.rs:110-117`) does not either. Adding stripping for a prefix neither
   130	  producer emits would be speculative code with an untestable branch. Task 2 records this in a
   131	  comment beside the normalizer instead of implementing it.
   132	
   133	## Flagged assumption (spec-less probe fallback, §C)
   134	
   135	AUTO-02's probe row came back `{"category":"concurrency","status":"unresolved","probe":"If
   136	interrupted or run in parallel, what is guaranteed?"}`. Surfaced, not silently dropped:
   137	
   138	> **FLAGGED (AUTO-02, unresolved).** The probe classified AUTO-02 as a **concurrency** concern.
   139	> That looks like a misclassification: `affects_compiled_binary` is a pure `&str -> bool`
   140	> transform with no shared state, no I/O and no interruption point, so "if interrupted or run
   141	> in parallel, what is guaranteed?" has no meaningful answer for it. This plan records that
   142	> judgement rather than inventing a concurrency edge to satisfy the probe. **No concurrency
   143	> acceptance criterion was authored from this row.** If a reviewer believes there IS a
   144	> concurrency surface here — the nearest candidate is `enforce_build_staleness` reading
   145	> `git status --porcelain` while another process mutates the worktree, which is pre-existing and
   146	> out of AUTO-02's scope — raise it before accepting this plan.
   147	
   148	No-silent-drop accounting for this plan: 1 probe-surfaced item = 0 authored into `truths` from
   149	the probe + 1 surfaced as a flagged assumption.
   150	
   151	**Canon-referral breadcrumb (§B):** "a crafted path escaping the workspace prefix via `..`
   152	segments" was recalled and is canon path-traversal, so it is DROPPED from
   153	`must_haves.prohibitions` per the canon-referral rule. Task 1 still adds `crates/../foo.rs` as
   154	an ordinary negative-control test case.
