  1091	/// [`preflight_unattended_launch_check`]'s body, with the report's destination
  1092	/// made injectable so a test can assert on the bytes actually emitted rather
  1093	/// than on a re-derivation of what they ought to be.
  1094	///
  1095	/// **This does not weaken D-09.** The one extra parameter is a byte sink; it
  1096	/// cannot reach the disposition, which is decided entirely by
  1097	/// [`ConditionState::refuses`] and `state.mode` below. The function callers
  1098	/// actually reach, and the only one wired into
  1099	/// [`generic_preflight_checks`], keeps the fixed `(&Path, &State)` signature.
  1100	///
  1101	/// A write failure on the sink is deliberately IGNORED rather than propagated:
  1102	/// a closed stdout must not convert a viable launch into a refusal, nor a
  1103	/// refusal into a pass. The disposition is computed from the conditions, never
  1104	/// from whether the report reached anyone.
  1105	fn unattended_launch_check_reporting_to(
  1106	    project_root: &Path,
  1107	    state: &State,
  1108	    report: &mut dyn std::io::Write,
  1109	) -> Result<(), String> {
  1110	    if !unattended_launch_check_applies(state.stage) {
  1111	        return Ok(());
