  1246	/// Gate a stage launch on readiness (17c, D-13-D-16): the generic universal
  1247	/// checks (D-14) plus the adapter-specific hook, called from `launch_stage`
  1248	/// BEFORE `monitor::spawn_monitor` so a readiness failure is caught before
  1249	/// any agent time is spent. A failing check is NEVER a hard exit — it
  1250	/// surfaces as a named preflight gate + notify (WR-11 idiom, D-15), mirroring
  1251	/// `handle_stage_failure`'s dispatch shape exactly.
  1252	///
  1253	/// Returns `Ok(true)` when the caller should continue the rest of
  1254	/// `launch_stage` (preflight passed). Returns `Ok(false)` when a failing
  1255	/// check was resolved via a gate that ALREADY completed a full retried
  1256	/// launch (Advance/LoopBack), reached the retry ceiling, or aborted —
  1257	/// the caller must not run any more launch steps for this invocation
  1258	/// (CR-01, 17-08 gap closure: the old `Result<(), CliError>` return
  1259	/// couldn't distinguish these cases, so the caller always continued and
  1260	/// spawned the agent a second time).

