   908	    // through to `advance` below. Both exits are covered because the guard is
   909	    // bound to a named variable in THIS scope; `let _ = ...` would drop it
   910	    // immediately and the flag's true-window would collapse to nothing.
   911	    //
   912	    // The target is `workdir`, not `project_root`: `.planning/config.json` is a
   913	    // tracked file inside the worktree the agent's cwd is set to, and that copy
   914	    // is the one GSD's `check auto-mode` reads.
   915	    //
   916	    // F-4 — no agent or launch-shape condition belongs in the predicate.
   917	    // `run_monitor` is the body of the hidden `__monitor` subcommand, which
   918	    // `monitor::spawn_monitor` re-execs ONLY on its `MonitorLaunch::PipeOwning`
   919	    // arm. Being inside this function already implies a stream launch (Claude
   920	    // and Antigravity today, round-3 D-10) — the old "Claude + stream launch"
   921	    // claim became false when the predicate widened — so re-checking
   922	    // `state.agent` or `state.legacy_claude_launch` here would be a second,
   923	    // driftable notion of the same fact. The consequence — a Legacy-arm or
   924	    // non-stream-agent launch never gets the flag — is accepted and is turned
   925	    // into a loud preflight refusal by plan `35.1-03`, not left silent.
   926	    //
   927	    // A state that will not load is NOT fatal here: warn, skip the guard, and
   928	    // let `advance` surface the real state error afterwards with its own
